<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Admins edit a dashboard by selecting it on the <a href="/manage/dashboards">Dashboards</a> list. It opens
        in preview, showing exactly what people will see.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Editing the layout">
        <ol>
            <li>Select the preview button in the toolbar to switch to editing.</li>
            <li>Use the + button to add a widget.</li>
            <li>Use the arrows on a widget to move it, and the size buttons to make it wider, narrower, taller or
                shorter. The grid is 12 columns wide.</li>
            <li>Right-click a widget to change its settings.</li>
            <li>Select the dashboard's name to rename it.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Save</strong>. Nothing is kept until you do.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Buttons and controls on widgets only work in preview. Widgets for features your company doesn't have
            are hidden in preview, but still shown while editing so you can remove them.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
            Deleting a dashboard can't be undone. If it was everyone's home screen, people go back to the
            standard home page.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
